{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310832,"nonce":"uZP9Cj61UeYo8Kf1b2GeGmFia+Y=","title":"Hub+spoke: session-scoped KV LANDED 4e637d77 (blocker 1 CLOSED, isolation proven). Dynamic growth is NOT the lever (7 MB = noise). Blockers ...","message":"**GOAL (user, 2026-08-19):** a hub + spoke harness where each spoke is a worker\nagent running CONCURRENTLY against one set of weights, engaging specific experts.\n\n**DYNAMIC KV GROWTH IS NOT THE LEVER — MEASURED AND REVERTED.** Implemented\ngeometric growth in `Q8Cache` (256-row window, double on demand, flat layout\npreserved so kernel row indexing is untouched). Result on Qwen2.5-0.5B:\n\n| | ctx=4096 | ctx=32768 |\n|---|---|---|\n| pre-sized | 307 MB | 319 MB |\n| dynamic | 306 MB | 312 MB |\n\n**7 MB, i.e. noise.** Mechanism confirms it: `haxe_bytes_alloc`\n(runtime/src/haxe_sys.rs:3279) uses `alloc_zeroed`, which for large blocks maps\nlazily, and macOS peak footprint counts TOUCHED pages. A pre-sized buffer costs\nADDRESS SPACE, not resident memory — and\n[[perf_peak_memory_levers_measured]] says \"~2.6 GB of **reservation**\", which I\nhad misread as resident. Growth would still matter on wasm (no lazy commit).\nReverted rather than ship unproven complexity.\n\n**THE THREE REAL BLOCKERS, verified in tree:**\n\n1. **~~KV IS MODEL STATE~~ — CLOSED 4e637d77. SESSION-SCOPED KV SHIPPED.**\n   `KVSession` (nue/nue/transformer/KVSession.hx) holds one `KVCache` per layer;\n   `LlamaModel.newSession()` builds one via `KVCache.cloneEmpty()`, and\n   `forwardIdsWith(ids, session)` decodes against it. `forwardWith(x, kv)` was\n   added to GQAttention and LlamaBlock; `forward(x)` delegates with the module's\n   own cache, so `Module`'s fixed `forward(x:Tensor):Tensor` signature is\n   untouched and EVERY EXISTING PATH IS UNCHANGED (llama-chat tokens diffed\n   identical before/after).\n   - **ORACLE**: `nue/examples/kv-session-smoke` — decode two conversations\n     sequentially, then a token at a time in turn; require exact agreement.\n     PASSES; model's own cache stays at 0. `GGUF=... ./run.sh`.\n   - **KVCache now remembers the REQUEST** (`reqQ8`/`reqHaxeQ8`/`numQHeads`)\n     because `useQ8`/`useQ8H` are the RESOLVED answers (downgrade on headDim%32\n     or plugin alloc failure) and cannot be replayed to build a matching cache.\n   - **The fused prefill graph is NOT taken on the session path** — it seeds the\n     model's own caches, which are not the session's. Session prefill runs the\n     per-op path until the graph can be told where to write.\n   - LANDMINE OBSERVED: KVCache's field comment says importers resolve its\n     fields BY DECLARATION ORDER — new fields must go after every existing one.\n\n   ORIGINAL DIAGNOSIS (kept for context): **KV IS MODEL STATE, NOT SESSION STATE.** `GQAttention.cache` is a field\n   (GQAttention.hx:46) built once in `LlamaArch.buildBlock` (`new KVCache(...)`).\n   Two concurrent spokes sharing a model interleave writes into ONE cache and\n   corrupt each other. Fix: thread a session through `forward` — the signatures\n   are `forward(x:Tensor)` on GQAttention/LlamaBlock and `forwardIds(ids)` on\n   LlamaModel, so this is a wide but mechanical change. A `model.bindSession()`\n   would avoid the churn but is NOT concurrency-safe (spokes race the binding).\n\n2. **THE SPIN POOL IS SINGLE-DISPATCHER.** `SpinPool.parallelRows` (one entry,\n   `compiler/haxe-std/rayzor/concurrent/SpinPool.hx:305`) distributes via ONE\n   shared atomic cursor with the CALLER participating. Two spokes dispatching\n   concurrently collide. Options: serialize dispatch across spokes (simplest,\n   and spokes are rarely all decoding at once), a pool per spoke with\n   cores/N workers each, or a multiplexing scheduler.\n\n3. **CONCURRENT SPOKES MULTIPLY THE EXPERT WORKING SET.** The 25-experts-per-\n   layer steady state in [[project_moe_expert_locality_measured]] is for ONE\n   stream. N spokes on DIFFERENT topics need roughly N x that resident before\n   the hit rate holds — 4 diverse spokes could push the expert cache from\n   ~1.2 GB to ~3.5 GB. Spokes on RELATED topics would share experts and cost\n   far less. **This is measurable with the routing harness already built**\n   (`scratchpad/capture_routing.py`): capture several prompts in ONE model load\n   and compute the union working set. Do that before sizing the cache.\n\n**ORDER I WOULD BUILD IT:** session-scoped KV first (it is the correctness\nblocker and unlocks everything), then measure multi-spoke expert locality, then\ndecide the pool story from how concurrent the spokes actually are.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_dynamic_kv_and_hub_spoke` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}